// numbers.anka: integer and float literals, and where they stop.
// C13  integers: 0 42 1000
// C14  floats: 3.14 0.5 2.5e-3 1e10 6E+2 2.5E0
// C15  ranges: 0..5 -> INT DOTDOT INT;  1.5..2 -> FLOAT DOTDOT INT;  1...5 -> INT DOTDOT ERROR INT
// C16  leading zeros: 007 and 00 are errors; 007.5 is a FLOAT (allowed, spec §2.4)
// C17  lone dot: 1. -> INT + ERROR '.';  .5 -> ERROR '.' + INT
// C18  number then letters: 123abc -> INT IDENT;  0x1F -> INT IDENT;  1e -> INT IDENT
// C19  no negative literals: -5 -> MINUS INT;  -2.5 -> MINUS FLOAT

0 42 1000
3.14 0.5 2.5e-3 1e10 6E+2 2.5E0
0..5 1.5..2 1...5
007 00 007.5
1. .5
123abc 0x1F 1e
-5 -2.5
